WEBVTT

00:16.307 --> 00:18.268
Aren't you going to eat anything?

00:31.364 --> 00:33.283
What the hell are you all doing?

00:34.576 --> 00:37.203
- Sir.
- Is this the time to be sleeping?

00:37.704 --> 00:39.497
Hello, sir.

00:41.249 --> 00:42.625
What about the warrant?

00:43.877 --> 00:45.879
We weren't able to request it yet.

00:46.838 --> 00:48.381
Wasn't the murder site found?

00:48.965 --> 00:52.552
Well, we found some evidence, but…

00:53.053 --> 00:55.513
It's pretty much like we didn't.

00:56.014 --> 00:57.515
- Yes.
- What are you saying?

00:58.016 --> 00:59.225
Where's Park Mu-gyeong?

01:01.895 --> 01:02.979
Sir.

01:04.022 --> 01:07.609
What the hell have you been doing?
What's your plan for the warrant?

01:07.692 --> 01:11.154
The prosecutor on duty
was one of the Boudoir's purchasers.

01:11.738 --> 01:14.407
She got arrested
knowing the warrant would be denied.

01:15.241 --> 01:16.701
- Bring the suspect.
- What?

01:16.785 --> 01:17.619
Yes, sir.

01:18.328 --> 01:19.537
Why, that little…

01:20.121 --> 01:20.955
Coffee?

01:35.011 --> 01:35.929
What about me?

01:36.012 --> 01:37.388
Have a cup of coffee.

01:45.146 --> 01:46.147
This is nice.

01:46.981 --> 01:48.775
There isn't much time left.

01:48.858 --> 01:50.610
Not for you, there isn't.

01:55.031 --> 01:57.325
I wondered why
you'd come here on your own.

01:58.201 --> 01:59.828
You voluntarily got arrested…

02:02.038 --> 02:03.915
so that you'd be released.

02:05.166 --> 02:06.751
I'm not the killer, that's why.

02:06.835 --> 02:10.922
We can't prove you faked your death
and tried to live as someone else.

02:11.005 --> 02:13.133
You came here,
so you're not a flight risk.

02:13.216 --> 02:17.512
And the DNA analysis proved
that you weren't the killer.

02:18.012 --> 02:19.806
I won't be requesting a warrant.

02:21.391 --> 02:23.143
It'll be denied anyway.

02:23.643 --> 02:26.437
What about the injustice
I've suffered in here?

02:26.521 --> 02:28.231
Who will compensate me for that?

02:30.108 --> 02:31.818
I'm the victim here.

02:33.194 --> 02:35.071
And you're the perpetrator.

02:35.155 --> 02:36.156
"The victim"?

02:38.575 --> 02:40.493
Speaking of which,

02:40.994 --> 02:43.955
it seems you and the victim
were very close.

02:44.038 --> 02:45.331
Why pretend not to know her?

03:03.558 --> 03:04.392
What's up?

03:05.268 --> 03:08.396
The victim really came here
from the boutique?

03:08.479 --> 03:09.939
The taxi company verified it.

03:10.023 --> 03:12.400
- Search the place. Now.
- Yes, sir.

03:21.326 --> 03:23.411
We're not finding prints or anything.

03:25.747 --> 03:28.374
It's far too clean here too.
There's nothing.

03:29.042 --> 03:31.336
It looks like everything's been wiped.

03:38.259 --> 03:40.094
Come check over here, please.

03:44.807 --> 03:49.354
PARKING GARAGE

03:49.437 --> 03:50.355
Excuse me.

03:50.855 --> 03:51.898
Do you work here?

03:52.398 --> 03:53.233
Yes.

03:53.316 --> 03:55.193
- Police.
- Right.

03:55.777 --> 03:59.656
Did you ever see the people
working in the next building over?

04:00.490 --> 04:02.700
The place should be empty right now.

04:03.201 --> 04:06.621
Everyone got taken away
in a recent immigration raid.

04:07.205 --> 04:08.456
When was that?

04:10.416 --> 04:12.627
Maybe, like, ten days ago?

04:21.094 --> 04:22.428
Your hand…

04:22.512 --> 04:24.889
- Sorry?
- The calluses on your hand.

04:26.849 --> 04:30.103
This? It's from using
a leather skiving knife for years.

04:30.603 --> 04:32.272
It's a garment cutter's mark.

04:40.989 --> 04:43.157
The victim worked at a bag factory,

04:43.241 --> 04:46.244
and those who could verify that
have been deported.

04:48.037 --> 04:49.664
This is the first I've heard of it.

04:50.164 --> 04:51.624
The boutique told us

04:52.292 --> 04:55.503
the dead person was Sarah Kim.

04:56.796 --> 04:57.630
Then

04:58.423 --> 05:00.550
was the victim impersonating Sarah Kim?

05:01.050 --> 05:04.637
Or are you impersonating the victim
right now?

05:05.722 --> 05:07.890
Choi Chae-u said the same thing.

05:08.891 --> 05:13.187
That the impersonator killed Sarah Kim.

05:15.606 --> 05:19.027
Then who's the person
sitting in front of me?

05:24.782 --> 05:26.034
How interesting.

05:28.202 --> 05:29.996
I'm Sarah Kim, of course.

05:30.079 --> 05:31.331
Prove it.

05:33.708 --> 05:35.084
You probably can't.

05:35.585 --> 05:38.588
It really doesn't matter
since both are fake anyway.

05:38.671 --> 05:40.214
I told you I'm Sarah Kim.

05:40.298 --> 05:42.008
Sarah Kim does not exist.

05:43.176 --> 05:48.389
You've been impersonating Sarah Kim,
who doesn't exist.

05:50.558 --> 05:51.726
No, that's not it.

05:51.809 --> 05:53.186
Then the victim found out

05:53.269 --> 05:56.189
you were an unregistered person
with no identity.

05:57.231 --> 06:00.360
- No.
- You pretended to be Sarah Kim perfectly.

06:00.443 --> 06:04.781
And thanks to that,
staging a murder was also easy for you.

06:06.074 --> 06:10.244
The victim had planned to kill you
from the start.

06:10.328 --> 06:13.956
But you managed to use that plan
to your advantage.

06:15.249 --> 06:17.293
Because you wanted to live as Sarah Kim.

06:26.511 --> 06:27.804
How will you prove that?

06:28.513 --> 06:30.515
I'll make you prove it yourself.

06:33.684 --> 06:35.686
Did you like the coffee?

06:36.187 --> 06:38.689
I bought it
near the broadcasting station in Sangam.

06:39.857 --> 06:43.236
You were arrested two days ago
at 6:05 p.m.,

06:43.319 --> 06:45.822
so you can watch it
right when you get out.

06:47.407 --> 06:49.033
The prime time news tonight

06:50.451 --> 06:52.495
will cover the Boudoir scam.

06:55.123 --> 06:57.875
I have people from news outlets
among my clients too.

06:59.043 --> 07:00.962
I told you.

07:01.045 --> 07:03.923
Nobody would be willing
to become victims of fraud.

07:05.341 --> 07:08.719
This is the notebook of Woo Hyo-eun,
former Boudoir manager.

07:09.512 --> 07:10.972
It's all here.

07:11.055 --> 07:13.057
From the names of your clients

07:13.558 --> 07:16.144
to sensitive details
they'd rather not reveal.

07:17.061 --> 07:20.773
How will people react
once the Boudoir scam is exposed?

07:21.899 --> 07:24.193
Secrets come to light in the end,

07:24.277 --> 07:26.237
people leave all too readily,

07:26.737 --> 07:28.656
the truth is always brutal,

07:29.907 --> 07:32.118
and illusions are bound to shatter.

07:40.835 --> 07:42.420
To shake you…

07:44.755 --> 07:47.383
I had no choice but to shake up Boudoir.

07:49.385 --> 07:51.846
Are detectives allowed
to arbitrarily leak case info?

07:52.346 --> 07:54.807
You'll be terminated now, not demoted.

07:54.891 --> 07:56.434
I told you I'd go all the way.

07:58.644 --> 08:00.313
Are you trying to die together?

08:01.063 --> 08:02.815
I'm just chasing a criminal.

08:02.899 --> 08:04.650
If you stop, I stop.

08:10.406 --> 08:11.532
Perhaps…

08:13.367 --> 08:15.953
Boudoir could've been real.

08:19.290 --> 08:20.917
If you had been real.

08:23.294 --> 08:24.837
But you're a fake,

08:25.838 --> 08:27.798
and that made Boudoir fake.

08:30.468 --> 08:32.762
You don't have much time left now.

08:45.733 --> 08:49.028
The so-called "Boudoir-gate"
is causing a stir.

08:49.529 --> 08:54.033
No one doubted its authenticity
until the fraud was exposed.

08:54.116 --> 08:57.995
People were deceived by the illusion
of limited editions and VIP status…

08:58.079 --> 09:01.541
That bitch behind the Boudoir fraud
should be executed.

09:01.624 --> 09:03.000
Get lost, seriously.

09:03.084 --> 09:04.835
Why do you live like this?

09:05.336 --> 09:06.587
Are you a fucking idiot?

09:06.671 --> 09:08.548
Flaunting is a sign of insecurity.

09:08.631 --> 09:11.384
Imitating someone like that
is a form of mental illness.

09:11.467 --> 09:15.555
How pathetic and miserable do you have
to be to steal someone else's life?

09:15.638 --> 09:17.557
All you'll ever be is an imitation.

10:03.227 --> 10:05.229
Secrets come to light in the end,

10:05.813 --> 10:07.982
people leave all too readily,

10:08.482 --> 10:10.818
and illusions are bound to shatter.

10:11.944 --> 10:12.862
Perhaps

10:13.487 --> 10:15.906
Boudoir could've been real.

10:16.407 --> 10:18.117
If you had been real.

10:50.191 --> 10:51.859
Voluntary appearance and confession.

10:52.360 --> 10:54.403
- That may reduce a sentence.
- How are they doing?

10:54.487 --> 10:55.446
They just began.

10:55.529 --> 10:57.782
Cooperating and showing genuine remorse

10:58.282 --> 11:00.076
may act as mitigating factors.

11:01.327 --> 11:03.412
This is the extent I can help you.

11:04.246 --> 11:05.956
The rest is up to you.

11:06.957 --> 11:08.584
I've already decided.

11:10.336 --> 11:12.588
The real thing needs no explanation,

11:14.131 --> 11:16.509
and fakes can't exist without one.

11:18.928 --> 11:20.388
Which is why

11:22.181 --> 11:24.975
I have a lot to explain, starting now.

11:46.330 --> 11:47.289
Excuse me.

11:48.582 --> 11:49.750
Excuse me.

11:52.670 --> 11:53.671
Can I help you?

11:54.588 --> 11:56.298
Is the factory manager here?

11:58.843 --> 12:01.470
They're on a long business trip overseas.

12:06.767 --> 12:09.270
- Can I sit for a bit before I go?
- Sure.

12:09.353 --> 12:10.521
Thank you.

12:14.608 --> 12:19.238
It's not easy to find a factory
that handles leather goods well.

12:19.780 --> 12:21.449
Because it's not profitable.

12:22.366 --> 12:23.951
You speak Korean well.

12:24.618 --> 12:26.537
Because I need to earn money.

12:37.047 --> 12:39.008
Your feet must hurt. Use this.

12:40.926 --> 12:42.094
Thank you.

12:44.764 --> 12:46.182
You make knockoffs here.

12:46.265 --> 12:47.266
Sorry?

12:51.187 --> 12:52.730
Your manager was taken away for it.

12:52.813 --> 12:54.732
Excuse me. No, wait.

12:54.815 --> 12:56.400
It's okay. I won't report you.

12:57.902 --> 12:59.820
It's fine. I'll just take a look.

13:04.116 --> 13:04.950
Wow.

13:21.801 --> 13:23.886
This is more than just okay. It's…

13:26.055 --> 13:27.723
Who made this one?

13:36.482 --> 13:37.525
Are you Korean?

13:40.319 --> 13:41.654
What's your name?

13:50.913 --> 13:52.498
Kim Mi-jeong.

13:53.123 --> 13:55.251
Want to make a handbag together?

13:59.338 --> 14:02.174
But how do you tell
the fake and real ones apart?

14:04.593 --> 14:08.722
Burning them is the easiest way.

14:09.223 --> 14:11.809
Synthetic leather deforms
in an ugly way as it burns.

14:11.892 --> 14:13.811
The real thing chars, turning into ash.

14:14.728 --> 14:16.397
But since that's hard to do,

14:16.480 --> 14:17.898
we listen to the zipper.

14:18.566 --> 14:19.984
"Listen"?

14:20.568 --> 14:22.653
The real ones even sound different.

14:23.153 --> 14:24.446
Want to listen?

14:48.554 --> 14:49.930
I'll go with this one.

14:55.811 --> 14:57.479
You have good instincts.

14:59.607 --> 15:03.569
This is a product
used by Goyard and Loro Piana.

15:15.497 --> 15:18.042
Sir, do you have anything
of better quality?

15:19.293 --> 15:20.878
All right, follow me.

15:28.677 --> 15:29.511
Here.

15:30.346 --> 15:32.473
What do young people know?

15:32.556 --> 15:34.558
They make great faux leather these days.

15:34.642 --> 15:37.186
If you guess which one is cowhide leather,

15:37.728 --> 15:39.104
I'll give you 10% off.

15:48.405 --> 15:50.741
I think it's the one on the left.

15:50.824 --> 15:52.326
See? You got it wrong.

15:52.826 --> 15:54.745
The one on the right is cowhide.

15:58.374 --> 15:59.375
What?

15:59.875 --> 16:01.085
You can't burn that!

16:01.168 --> 16:03.003
Burning it will tell me if it's fake.

16:04.672 --> 16:07.424
It's burning! Come on.

16:09.343 --> 16:10.678
So this one is real.

16:11.178 --> 16:14.264
Man, this may not be leather,
but it's still pricey.

16:19.353 --> 16:20.354
- Thank you.
- Enjoy.

16:20.437 --> 16:23.732
How did you know
the one on the right was fake?

16:24.775 --> 16:26.819
What would I know about leather?

16:27.611 --> 16:29.446
But I know how to read people.

16:35.661 --> 16:38.789
You seem different from other people.

16:39.915 --> 16:41.000
How so?

16:41.083 --> 16:43.836
You're supplying the bags to Dongdaemun,

16:44.420 --> 16:47.464
but you focus on every detail,
as if making luxury goods.

16:49.466 --> 16:51.635
I want to become like you.

16:55.472 --> 16:57.766
You must not know how to read people.

17:56.825 --> 17:58.160
I'm sorry.

17:58.243 --> 18:00.954
I shouldn't have changed the design
without asking.

18:02.664 --> 18:03.499
No.

18:04.750 --> 18:06.960
I've never seen anything better.

18:07.044 --> 18:08.003
- Wow!
- Wow.

18:08.087 --> 18:09.088
Mi-jeong.

18:09.171 --> 18:11.340
- Congratulations.
- Never disappoints.

18:15.219 --> 18:16.428
Who could that be?

18:16.929 --> 18:18.388
We're not expecting anyone.

18:19.389 --> 18:21.225
- I'll get it.
- Check who it is.

18:22.559 --> 18:24.645
Hide.

18:27.022 --> 18:28.065
It's me.

18:29.817 --> 18:31.068
It's Ms. Kim.

18:40.035 --> 18:41.912
It'd be a shame to just end things.

18:43.580 --> 18:44.623
Can I come in?

18:45.290 --> 18:46.125
This is tasty.

18:46.208 --> 18:48.210
Today is Boudoir's birthday!

18:52.089 --> 18:54.508
Happy Birthday!

18:54.591 --> 18:56.969
- Love you. Congratulations!
- Blow it out.

18:59.763 --> 19:00.931
Thank you.

19:01.014 --> 19:03.183
- Congratulations.
- We love you.

19:04.643 --> 19:07.104
Production will start
as soon as I get the investment.

19:08.897 --> 19:10.899
I'll leave things in your trusted hands.

19:14.611 --> 19:16.822
I'm only good at making replicas.

19:17.531 --> 19:19.032
It's fake talent.

19:21.201 --> 19:23.162
If you can't tell the fake from the real,

19:23.662 --> 19:24.997
is it really fake?

19:29.001 --> 19:33.255
I'll give you a generous advance payment,
so let's work together for a long time.

19:37.801 --> 19:38.802
Can you

19:40.095 --> 19:41.889
give that to me in cash?

19:43.390 --> 19:45.392
Cash is convenient and simple.

19:45.934 --> 19:47.186
May I ask why?

19:53.525 --> 19:56.361
Also, you're young
and working at a place like this.

19:57.446 --> 19:59.031
Are you on the run?

20:00.949 --> 20:02.492
It's not that different.

20:04.077 --> 20:05.787
I was actually joking.

20:08.832 --> 20:11.335
I ran away from home at a very young age.

20:11.835 --> 20:15.589
I couldn't get a resident card,
so I couldn't open a bank account.

20:20.302 --> 20:21.637
I'm not that different.

20:22.846 --> 20:23.805
What do you mean?

20:23.889 --> 20:25.432
The running away part.

20:34.066 --> 20:35.651
Give it to me here.

20:37.444 --> 20:40.489
Mi-jeong, can you take a look at this?

20:41.698 --> 20:43.575
Like this, right?

20:46.787 --> 20:49.456
No, I got the dates mixed up.

20:51.291 --> 20:52.459
Hurry up!

20:56.380 --> 20:58.548
You just need to check
my measurements, right?

20:59.383 --> 21:00.300
Mi-jeong.

21:00.842 --> 21:02.010
I understand.

21:03.512 --> 21:05.180
Can you do me a favor?

21:05.264 --> 21:06.723
Sure. What do you need?

21:06.807 --> 21:09.309
Can you do a fitting for me
at the boutique?

21:09.893 --> 21:13.397
I barely managed to make a reservation,
but I accidentally double-booked.

21:13.480 --> 21:14.856
You want me to go?

21:15.524 --> 21:18.026
They need my measurements
as it's my first time.

21:18.110 --> 21:19.820
Where did my wallet go?

21:19.903 --> 21:21.655
I have money too.

21:24.366 --> 21:25.284
Come here.

21:26.743 --> 21:29.246
We're the same height
and have similar builds.

21:32.582 --> 21:34.793
Don't you think we look quite alike?

21:38.463 --> 21:41.049
I don't think we look alike at all.

21:43.260 --> 21:45.137
Say my name, and they'll do everything.

21:50.934 --> 21:53.061
What name is the reservation under?

21:55.731 --> 21:57.190
It's Sarah Kim.

22:03.655 --> 22:05.866
I seem like a different person.

22:06.366 --> 22:08.577
This is what you really look like.

22:10.954 --> 22:13.165
Maybe it's because
I've heard so much about you,

22:13.248 --> 22:15.625
but I feel like I know you already.

22:16.710 --> 22:18.837
Actually, I'm…

22:18.920 --> 22:20.380
- Here.
- Okay.

22:21.089 --> 22:23.467
Shall we try on the earrings too?

22:35.854 --> 22:37.230
May I call you Sarah?

22:39.149 --> 22:39.983
Sure.

22:40.776 --> 22:42.277
Time to eat. What do you want?

22:42.361 --> 22:43.653
Let's go to eat.

22:44.154 --> 22:46.239
Let's go eat, Mi-jeong.

22:46.323 --> 22:47.407
Go ahead.

23:35.372 --> 23:36.456
Mi-jeong.

23:39.459 --> 23:40.377
It's a gift.

23:41.962 --> 23:43.630
That's my number, so save it.

23:44.756 --> 23:46.007
Here. Come with me.

24:05.986 --> 24:09.197
You can learn the world
without going to college.

24:10.198 --> 24:11.450
Thank you.

24:12.075 --> 24:13.785
For the phone too.

24:13.869 --> 24:17.122
I figured you wouldn't have one
if you didn't have a bank account.

24:19.082 --> 24:20.917
I'm lending you my name briefly.

24:23.462 --> 24:26.047
Call me if you need stronger meds
than aspirin.

24:27.007 --> 24:28.925
If you don't have an account or phone,

24:30.302 --> 24:33.180
you probably never even visited a doctor
when you were sick.

24:36.641 --> 24:37.767
Why are you

24:38.810 --> 24:40.270
so nice to me?

24:45.775 --> 24:47.402
You remind me…

24:49.404 --> 24:51.615
of someone I know.

26:01.142 --> 26:03.186
No, you must be mistaken.

26:03.728 --> 26:05.647
I told you I've never used my card there.

26:05.730 --> 26:08.775
The impersonation went on
for over six months, but no one knew.

26:08.858 --> 26:10.485
Many had heard the name,

26:10.569 --> 26:13.280
but only a handful knew
what Sarah Kim looked like.

26:14.614 --> 26:16.408
That's possible for others,

26:16.908 --> 26:18.660
but you must've known.

26:21.955 --> 26:24.457
It is not lies that blind us.

26:25.917 --> 26:27.127
It's trust.

26:29.504 --> 26:32.340
There wasn't a single honest person
in this relationship…

26:34.843 --> 26:36.761
but we trusted each other too much.

26:45.937 --> 26:47.188
What was that?

27:19.304 --> 27:23.183
If you can't tell the fake from the real,
is it really fake?

27:23.266 --> 27:25.435
If you can't tell the fake from the real,

27:26.269 --> 27:27.646
is it really fake?

27:29.773 --> 27:32.233
If you can't tell the fake from the real,

27:32.317 --> 27:34.402
is it really fake?

27:44.954 --> 27:47.916
If you can't tell the fake from the real,

27:49.042 --> 27:50.960
is it really fake?

27:54.297 --> 27:56.800
If you can't tell the fake from the real…

28:01.429 --> 28:02.514
Ms. Kim?

28:05.433 --> 28:07.268
Can I come in for a bit?

28:40.176 --> 28:42.262
Can I ask what's wrong?

28:42.929 --> 28:44.139
I just…

28:46.141 --> 28:48.643
didn't pay back the money
I borrowed from a friend,

28:49.644 --> 28:51.479
and so I got beaten up.

28:54.357 --> 28:58.027
Trusting something trustworthy is easy.

28:58.653 --> 29:01.448
But trusting someone
even in an impossible moment?

29:01.948 --> 29:03.700
That's real trust.

29:06.494 --> 29:08.371
I trust you.

29:11.666 --> 29:13.376
It felt like

29:14.586 --> 29:16.421
I was the one talking just now.

29:19.382 --> 29:20.216
Did it?

29:21.634 --> 29:25.180
They say people start talking alike
when they grow close.

29:56.127 --> 29:57.545
Those earrings.

29:59.172 --> 30:00.924
They're the same as mine.

30:06.721 --> 30:07.722
They don't really

30:08.556 --> 30:10.099
suit me, do they?

30:10.683 --> 30:12.227
No, they suit you well.

30:15.230 --> 30:18.274
You know, fakes look
like the real thing nowadays.

30:21.402 --> 30:22.237
And this.

30:24.489 --> 30:25.740
You have it.

30:25.824 --> 30:27.659
I don't need it anymore.

30:29.244 --> 30:30.620
Thank you.

30:31.120 --> 30:31.996
But…

30:34.207 --> 30:36.584
why do you assume these are fake?

30:42.841 --> 30:44.300
May we have a word with you?

30:44.384 --> 30:48.179
We need to check a matter
regarding the membership card you used.

30:51.891 --> 30:53.268
Don't you know who I am?

30:53.768 --> 30:54.936
I'm Sarah Kim.

30:55.019 --> 30:57.313
The card you used was reported stolen.

30:57.814 --> 30:59.190
Please come with us.

30:59.858 --> 31:01.401
Whatever, damn it.

31:02.235 --> 31:03.903
Let go. I said let go.

31:04.404 --> 31:05.238
Let go!

31:11.119 --> 31:13.913
The card owner wants
to resolve this amicably.

31:13.997 --> 31:15.832
She says to just let her go.

31:18.835 --> 31:21.379
She's just letting me go?

31:22.630 --> 31:23.631
Man.

31:24.632 --> 31:26.050
Consider yourself lucky.

31:26.551 --> 31:28.887
Seems the owner prefers
not to involve the police.

31:36.769 --> 31:38.605
She's not reporting me?

31:40.106 --> 31:41.024
But why?

31:51.159 --> 31:53.328
JULIET WITH A GUN

32:29.781 --> 32:31.866
I've never seen anything better.

32:33.451 --> 32:34.327
This bag.

32:35.244 --> 32:36.371
How much is it?

32:36.871 --> 32:38.247
It's 50 million won.

32:38.331 --> 32:41.167
It's our most popular steady seller.

32:42.669 --> 32:47.006
Its unique stitches are made possible
by the delicate craftsmanship

32:47.090 --> 32:48.758
of a seasoned artisan.

32:49.258 --> 32:50.927
It's one of the reasons

32:51.427 --> 32:54.347
it's considered a work of art,
not just a handbag.

33:03.064 --> 33:04.691
"A work of art"?

33:05.191 --> 33:06.651
Yes, that's correct.

33:07.568 --> 33:09.404
I made that.

33:11.739 --> 33:13.324
I'm the one who made that.

33:25.086 --> 33:26.170
Ms. Kim?

33:34.721 --> 33:37.015
It was you. You've been impersonating me.

33:38.725 --> 33:40.977
Why did you go through my room?

33:41.060 --> 33:43.521
It was you, of all people.

33:45.106 --> 33:48.818
There were all those rumors
about how I was vulgar and nouveau riche.

33:49.402 --> 33:51.029
That was you.

33:52.613 --> 33:53.906
Can't I do that?

33:55.450 --> 33:59.245
Why can't I have what you have?

34:00.413 --> 34:02.498
We promised to work together
for a long time.

34:02.582 --> 34:03.833
"A long time"?

34:03.916 --> 34:05.043
"Together"?

34:08.796 --> 34:11.466
Then you shouldn't have gotten in my way.

34:11.966 --> 34:14.135
You should've imitated me properly.

34:15.595 --> 34:17.722
And at this vital time. How dare you…

34:17.805 --> 34:20.725
You shouldn't talk to me that way.

34:20.808 --> 34:22.685
Not after all I've done for you.

34:23.603 --> 34:24.729
You're fired.

34:25.354 --> 34:27.523
Quietly pack your stuff and leave.

34:27.607 --> 34:30.234
Weren't we indispensable to each other?

34:32.904 --> 34:34.447
Why would you ruin that?

34:36.199 --> 34:38.117
Keep acting in desperation like that.

34:46.667 --> 34:47.668
"Desperation"?

34:51.214 --> 34:52.423
She stole her name…

34:59.180 --> 35:01.349
isolated her from those around her…

35:02.475 --> 35:06.395
Immigration office?
I'd like to report illegal immigrants.

35:06.479 --> 35:08.689
…got rid of those who knew them…

35:21.160 --> 35:23.246
erased the traces
that would identify them…

35:34.924 --> 35:36.467
Desperation.

35:38.177 --> 35:39.929
Fuck.

35:41.848 --> 35:44.225
…and became the perfect Sarah Kim.

35:46.686 --> 35:48.729
Are you admitting to the murder?

35:55.987 --> 35:57.363
I killed her.

35:57.864 --> 35:58.990
Okay!

35:59.574 --> 36:00.533
We got her.

36:04.036 --> 36:06.247
Serenity is the only gift of confession.

36:07.290 --> 36:09.458
I hope you can find peace now.

36:12.128 --> 36:15.173
- That concludes the interrogation--
- I impersonated her.

36:16.340 --> 36:18.676
And I killed her to become Sarah Kim.

36:23.139 --> 36:24.348
My name is…

36:28.186 --> 36:29.896
Kim Mi-jeong.

36:36.110 --> 36:38.446
KIM MI-JEONG

36:41.741 --> 36:44.702
THE ART OF SARAH

38:10.788 --> 38:15.793
Subtitle translation by: Yung Un Choi
